      {
        "id": "s1",
        "title": "Search the sorted values",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "s1b1",
            "code": "def binary_search(values, target):\n    low = 0\n    high = len(values) - 1"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1b2",
            "code": "    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1b3",
            "code": "        if values[mid] == target:\n            return mid"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1b4",
            "code": "        if values[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1b5",
            "code": "        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return -1"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1b6",
            "code": "\nvalues = [1, 3, 5, 7, 9]\nprint(binary_search(values, 7))"
          }
        ],
        "explanation": "Start with low and high around all five values. The first middle value is 5 at index 2, so move low to index 3 because 7 must be to the right. The next middle value is 7 at index 3, so return that index. The final two lines run this exact example and print 3.",
        "typeAlongRanges": [
          {
            "endLine": 12,
            "startLine": 4
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
